  - name: gaia_client
    type: baseCOMP
    parameters:
      parentshortcut: GaiaClient
      opshortcut: Gaia
    custom_pars:
      Config:
      - name: Brokerhost
        style: Str
        label: Broker Host
        startSection: true
        default: 192.168.1.142
        help: MQTT broker IP address for Gaia's LAN broker (mosquitto). Not localhost -- point this at the actual Gaia broker host for the deployment.
      - name: Brokerport
        style: Int
        label: Broker Port
        default: 1883
        help: MQTT broker TCP port. Standard unencrypted MQTT port is 1883.
      - name: Tailscalehost
        style: Str
        label: Tailscale Host
        default: core-node-0.tail62079e.ts.net
        help: 'Optional fallback broker host (Tailscale hostname or IP) used ONLY when the LAN is unreachable: neither mqtt_ingest nor mqtt_device is connected AND no beacon reply has been heard for ~90s. Beacon Discovery''s LAN self-correction always stays primary -- this never overrides a reachable LAN broker, and does nothing (stays disconnected, never blocks) if left blank. GAIA_INTERFACE.md section 3 (Gaia Agent Universale, 2026-08-29).'
      - name: Deviceid
        style: Str
        label: Device ID
        startSection: true
        help: 'Gaia device registry identity, published as gaia/device/{id}/status. Leave blank to auto-generate ''td-{project name}-{6-char hash of the project''s absolute folder}'' (gaia_device_agent.py _read_config/_project_key) -- stable across restarts, and distinct even when two different projects share a .toe filename. Was previously hostname-based (td-{hostname}), which collided when multiple TD instances ran on the same machine -- fixed 2026-08-28. Set this explicitly (and uniquely) only for the one case auto-generation can''t disambiguate: two live TD processes launched off the EXACT SAME project folder at once. If you DO set it by hand for any other reason, follow the Gaia convention (GAIA_INTERFACE.md section 1d): lowercase, dashes only, td-{family}-{machine}[-{rig}] -- e.g. td-patchdeck-macmauro, td-dmx-ops-a.'
        value: td-dmx-win
      - name: Stanza
        style: Str
        label: Room
        help: 'Room/zone this TD instance claims in Gaia''s roomGraph (room_claim on announce). Leave blank if not tied to a specific physical room. Rooms Gaia''s room graph currently recognizes: soggiorno, salotto, cucina, ingresso, corridoio, studio (touring installs have their own, e.g. palazzo-ducale) -- a name outside that set is harmless but won''t connect to anything on the Gaia side.'
        value: ConsolleDmx
      - name: Name
        style: Str
        label: Display Name
        default: GaiaClient
        help: Human-readable display name shown in Gaia's Pi Manager/device list.
        value: DMXRIG
      - name: Family
        style: Str
        help: Gaia project family -- declares WHICH TD PROJECT this instance belongs to (e.g. 'dmx', 'patchdeck', 'gaia'), shared by every instance of that project. Distinct from Deviceid, which identifies the individual instance -- Deviceid distinguishes the instance, Family distinguishes the project. Feeds the channel-5 matrix topic name (gaia/devices/{id}/{family}_matrix, built in the project-specific services script, not gaia_client itself) and is included in the status/profile MQTT payloads so Gaia-side consumers (Admin, watchdog) can group/filter by project without hand-maintained device_id lists or regexes. Always lowercase (GAIA_INTERFACE.md section 1b) -- gaia_device_agent.py normalizes it automatically, but type it lowercase so what you see here matches what gets published. Leave blank only if this instance intentionally has no channel-5 matrix to publish.
        value: dmx
      Services:
      - name: Canvasingest
        style: Toggle
        label: Canvas Ingest
        startSection: true
        default: true
        help: Enable ingest of gaia/td/canvas, gaia/brain/state, gaia/brain/dream MQTT topics into topic_canvas/topic_brainstate/topic_dream and their derived soul/lexicon/thought outputs. The MQTT connection itself always stays up when the component is active; this only gates whether incoming messages are stored/processed -- never toggle mqttclientDAT.par.active directly, that has crashed TD before.
      - name: Devicestatus
        style: Toggle
        label: Device Status
        help: 'Enable Gaia device registry: periodic gaia/device/{id}/status heartbeat, gaia/devices/{id}/announce+profile, and remote enable/disable/restart/set commands. Disabling this stops publishing/command handling but keeps the MQTT connection alive (same crash-avoidance reasoning as Canvas Ingest).'
        value: true
      - name: Reregister
        style: Pulse
        label: Re-register Services
        help: Manually retries the project's service/param registration (whatever was passed to gaia_device_agent.register_project_registrar() -- e.g. PatchDeck's register_all()) without restarting TD. Same recovery this component already does automatically when the registry is found empty (self-check in tick()); use this to force it immediately instead of waiting. No-op (logged) if the project never called register_project_registrar(). GAIA_INTERFACE.md section 2.
      - name: Mocapingest
        style: Toggle
        label: Direct Mocap Ingest (OSC)
        help: 'Enable direct OSC mocap ingest from a Gaia OPS node running mediapipe_node.py (face/hand/pose landmarks on UDP port 7000). Requires Devicestatus enabled too -- the OPS node discovers this TD instance''s IP via the device status heartbeat. Safe to toggle live: gates an OSC In CHOP, not a mqttclientDAT.'
      - name: Devicecontrol
        style: Toggle
        label: Device Fleet Control
        help: 'Enable Gaia fleet control: subscribe to gaia/device/+/status for ALL Gaia devices (not just this one), maintain a live devices_table (device_id/name/stanza/role/service/state/offline), and expose gaia_client_control.send_command(device_id, service, action) for enable/disable/restart. Independent of Device Status above -- that makes THIS instance a controllable device; this makes it a controller of the whole fleet. Ported from TD-Gaia''s td_service_control.py. No bundled UI panel -- bind a List COMP to devices_table in your own project to build one.'
        value: true
      - name: Beacondiscovery
        style: Toggle
        label: Broker Auto-Discovery (Beacon)
        help: 'Enable UDP broker self-correction: every 30s, probes whatever Brokerhost is currently set to on port 8899 with ''GAIA_DISCOVER''; if it answers as service==''gaia-core'', Brokerhost is corrected to the reported mqtt_host. Does nothing if that host doesn''t answer (no blind network-wide discovery -- verify a gaia_beacon responder exists on this deployment''s Gaia Core before enabling). Off by default so a deliberately-set Brokerhost is never silently overwritten.'
        value: true
      Mocap:
      - name: Opsdevice
        style: StrMenu
        label: OPS Device ID
        menuNames:
        - minipc-core-node-0
        menuLabels:
        - minipc-core-node-0 (salotto)
        help: 'Device id of the Gaia OPS node whose mediapipe_node.py sends direct mocap OSC (/gaia/mocap/{Opsdevice}/pose|hand|face/{person}). Now a menu: suggestions are populated live from gaia/device/+/status senders currently reporting osc_landmarks=true (see Mocap Senders Available below) -- still free text, type a value not in the list if you know it''s correct but hasn''t been seen recently. Must match the ACTUAL sender exactly or Mocap Status will say ''listening'' with zero data arriving (found live 2026-09-29).'
        value: minipc-core-node-0
      - name: Mocapsenders
        style: Str
        label: Mocap Senders Available
        readOnly: true
        help: 'Read-only: device_id list of every Gaia device currently reporting osc_landmarks=true in its gaia/device/{id}/status heartbeat (same 30s-heartbeat freshness as Device Fleet Control''s devices_table -- a sender missing for 90s drops off this list). Populated regardless of the Device Fleet Control toggle above (most single-purpose mocap installs run with that off). Pick one of these for Opsdevice above; ''none seen recently'' means no Gaia device is currently advertising mocap capability on this broker.'
        value: minipc-core-node-0
      - name: Mocapport
        style: Int
        label: Mocap OSC Port
        default: 7010
        help: 'UDP port oscin_mocap listens on for direct mocap OSC. Default 7010 (changed from 7000 on 2026-09-29 to stay clear of a host project''s own channel-1-style OSC In, which often defaults to 7000 too). Guarded: mocap_lifecycle.py bind-tests this port before activating -- if something OUTSIDE this TD process already holds it, ingest stays off and Mocapstatus (Status page) says why. Running multiple gaia_client instances in one project (e.g. one per rig) CAN share one Mocapport -- TD shares a port between its own operators with no error -- but give each instance a distinct Opsdevice or the OSC scope filtering does more redundant work than it needs to; a distinct Mocapport per instance avoids that entirely.'
      Status:
      - name: Identitystatus
        style: Str
        label: Identity Status
        default: ok
        readOnly: true
        help: 'Live check of Deviceid/Family -- ''ok'' when both are set, otherwise lists which are MISSING and the component tile turns red in the network editor. Never silently inherited from a clone: check this after copying/instancing gaia_client and set both explicitly before the copy goes live. GAIA_INTERFACE.md section 1/1b.'
      - name: Connectionstatus
        style: Str
        label: Connection Status
        startSection: true
        default: not connected
        readOnly: true
        help: Live MQTT connection state of the ingest client (mqtt_ingest), updated by mqtt_ingest_callbacks.
        value: connected
      - name: Lastmessage
        style: Str
        label: Last Message
        readOnly: true
        help: Topic and local time of the most recently received Gaia MQTT message.
        value: gaia/td/canvas @ 15:14:56
      - name: Deviceagentstatus
        style: Str
        label: Device Agent Status
        default: not connected
        readOnly: true
        help: Live MQTT connection state of the device-agent client (mqtt_device), updated by mqtt_device_callbacks. Separate from Connectionstatus above.
        value: connected
      - name: Beaconstatus
        style: Str
        label: Beacon Status
        default: not probed
        readOnly: true
        help: Outcome of the last broker auto-discovery probe (only active when Beacon Discovery is enabled).
        value: 'auto: 192.168.1.142 (beacon @ core-node-0, 13:10:39)'
      - name: Mocapstatus
        style: Str
        label: Mocap Status
        readOnly: true
        help: Direct Mocap Ingest (oscin_mocap) port-bind outcome, set by mocap_lifecycle.py's port guard. Blank when Mocapingest is off. 'listening on <port>' when the bind test passed and oscin_mocap is receiving. 'PORT <port> BUSY -- ...' when another listener already holds Mocapport (e.g. this project's own channel-1 OSC In) -- oscin_mocap is deliberately kept inactive rather than fail a bind silently; free the port or change Mocapport and it recovers on its own within ~10s.
    flags:
    - viewer
    position: [670, -430]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
    tags:
    - tox
    storage:
      lastmsg_seconds: 13329.1083333333
    children:
    - name: soul
      type: outCHOP
      parameters:
        label: 'Soul: mood_r/g/b, stress, calm, social, curiosity, energy, lifeindex'
      position: [2800, 700]
      color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
      inputs:
      - out_soul
    - name: word
      type: outDAT
      parameters:
        label: 'Word: current rotating word'
        connectorder: 4
      position: [2800, 100]
      inputs:
      - dat_word_current
      dat_read_only: true
    - name: mocap
      type: outCHOP
      parameters:
        label: 'Mocap: f* face, h* hand, p* pose, faces/hands/poses counts'
        connectorder: 1
      position: [2800, -1400]
      color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
      inputs:
      - merge_mocap
    - name: words
      type: outDAT
      parameters:
        label: 'Words: top lexicon table (word, count)'
        connectorder: 3
      position: [2800, 300]
      inputs:
      - dat_words
      dat_read_only: true
    - name: status
      type: outCHOP
      parameters:
        label: 'Status: connected, agent_connected, mocap_active, msg_age (s, -1 = none)'
        connectorder: 2
      position: [2800, -2200]
      color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
      inputs:
      - constant_status
    - name: thought
      type: outDAT
      parameters:
        label: 'Thought: latest LLM thought'
        connectorder: 5
      position: [2800, -100]
      inputs:
      - dat_thought
      dat_read_only: true
    - name: lag_soul
      type: lagCHOP
      parameters:
        lag1: 1.5
        lag2: 1.5
        autoexportroot: =parent()
      position: [1200, 700]
      size: [130, 90]
      color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
      inputs:
      - script_soul
    - name: out_soul
      type: nullCHOP
      position: [1600, 700]
      color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
      inputs:
      - lag_soul
    - name: chop_face
      type: scriptCHOP
      parameters:
        callbacks: chop_face_callbacks
      position: [800, -1000]
    - name: chop_hand
      type: scriptCHOP
      parameters:
        callbacks: chop_hand_callbacks
      position: [800, -1400]
    - name: chop_meta
      type: scriptCHOP
      parameters:
        callbacks: chop_meta_callbacks
      position: [800, -2200]
    - name: chop_pose
      type: scriptCHOP
      parameters:
        callbacks: chop_pose_callbacks
      position: [800, -1800]
    - name: dat_words
      type: scriptDAT
      parameters:
        callbacks: dat_words_callbacks
      position: [800, 300]
      dat_read_only: true
    - name: null_mocap
      type: nullCHOP
      position: [400, -1000]
      color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
      inputs:
      - oscin_mocap
    - name: dat_thought
      type: scriptDAT
      parameters:
        callbacks: dat_thought_callbacks
      position: [800, -100]
      dat_read_only: true
    - name: merge_mocap
      type: mergeCHOP
      position: [2400, -1400]
      inputs:
      - chop_face
      - chop_hand
      - chop_pose
      - chop_meta
    - name: mqtt_device
      type: mqttclientDAT
      parameters:
        netaddress: ="tcp://" + parent.GaiaClient.par.Brokerhost.eval() + ":" + str(int(parent.GaiaClient.par.Brokerport.eval()))
        usercid: =(parent.GaiaClient.par.Deviceid.eval() or ('td-' + str(me.id))) + '-device'
        callbacks: mqtt_device_callbacks
      position: [0, -3200]
      dat_read_only: true
    - name: mqtt_ingest
      type: mqttclientDAT
      parameters:
        netaddress: ="tcp://" + parent.GaiaClient.par.Brokerhost.eval() + ":" + str(int(parent.GaiaClient.par.Brokerport.eval()))
        usercid: =(parent.GaiaClient.par.Deviceid.eval() or ('td-' + str(me.id))) + '-ingest'
        callbacks: mqtt_ingest_callbacks
      position: [0, 700]
      dat_read_only: true
    - name: oscin_mocap
      type: oscinCHOP
      parameters:
        active: =op('mocap_lifecycle').module.resolveActive()
        port: =parent.GaiaClient.par.Mocapport.eval()
        oscaddressscope: ='/gaia/mocap/' + parent.GaiaClient.par.Opsdevice.eval() + '/*'
        autoexportroot: =parent()
      position: [0, -1000]
      size: [130, 90]
      color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
