    annotations:
    - name: annotate1
      mode: annotate
      title: Gaia MQTT Ingest -- Canvas / Brain State / Dream
      text: 'Subscribes gaia/td/canvas, gaia/brain/state, gaia/brain/dream and caches the raw JSON per topic. Derived Script CHOP/DAT outputs: soul mood (out_soul), top-20 lexicon words + rotating current word, latest LLM thought. Gated by Services > Canvas Ingest (logic-level gate -- the mqttclientDAT connection itself always stays up).'
      position: [-70, -290]
      size: [1870, 1250]
      color: [0.325, 0.5, 0.3]
    - name: annotate2
      mode: annotate
      title: Direct Mocap Ingest (OSC)
      text: 'Receives face/hand/pose/meta landmarks via OSC (port = Mocapport, default 7010, changed from 7000 2026-09-29 to avoid sharing a project''s own channel-1-style OSC In) from a Gaia OPS node''s mediapipe_node.py, scoped to /gaia/mocap/{Opsdevice}/*. Bounded, deterministic-slice extraction per channel family (unstable/unbounded raw addressing, no automatic expiry). Gated by Services > Direct Mocap Ingest -- oscin_mocap''s Active parameter is driven by mocap_lifecycle.py''s resolveActive() (bind-test guard), not a bare mirror of the toggle: refuses to activate and reports why in Mocapstatus if Mocapport is held by something OUTSIDE this TD process. Remotely controllable (2026-09-30): Mocapingest and Opsdevice are self-registered via register_param(), so Gaia Admin''s mocap Enable/Disable button can set both over the existing channel-4 command ({"action":"set","param":"Mocapingest"|"Opsdevice","value":...}) instead of requiring a manual edit inside TD -- Disable is symmetric (also sets Mocapingest false). Running 2+ gaia_client instances in one project (e.g. one per rig)? Give each a distinct Mocapport if more than one has mocap ingest enabled.'
      position: [-70, -2390]
      size: [1070, 1650]
      color: [0.3, 0.45, 0.55]
    - name: annotate3
      mode: annotate
      title: Device Registration (this instance as a controllable device)
      text: 'Publishes gaia/device/{id}/status heartbeat + gaia/devices/{id}/announce+profile, and accepts remote enable/disable/restart/set commands. Register real controls per-project via gaia_device_agent.module.register_service()/register_param() -- see its docstring. Gated by Services > Device Status (logic-level -- connection always stays up). WARNING: device_id defaults to td-{hostname}; do not run two Gaia device agents with the same device_id in the same project/network at once (they will fight over the same MQTT topic). reregister_watch fires the Services > Re-register pulse into gaia_device_agent.reregister() (GAIA_INTERFACE.md section 2) -- retries whatever project registrar was set via register_project_registrar() without restarting TD.'
      position: [-70, -3390]
      size: [1470, 450]
      color: [0.55, 0.45, 0.3]
    - name: annotate4
      mode: annotate
      title: Device Fleet Control + Broker Auto-Discovery
      text: 'Fleet control: subscribes gaia/device/+/status for ALL Gaia devices, maintains devices_table, exposes gaia_fleet_control.send_command(device_id, service, action). Gated by Services > Device Fleet Control. Same file also runs mocap sender discovery (2026-09-30, independent of the Device Fleet Control gate -- most mocap-only installs run that off): filters the same gaia/device/+/status stream for osc_landmarks==true and pushes live suggestions onto Mocap > OPS Device ID plus a Mocap Senders Available readout, so an operator sees who is actually sending mocap instead of guessing (see the operator tutorial above). Beacon discovery: broadcasts GAIA_DISCOVER on UDP 8899 (255.255.255.255, zero-config -- verified live 2026-09-29) every 30s to find Gaia Core on the local LAN and correct Brokerhost to its reported mqtt_host; falls back to Tailscalehost after ~90s of no LAN reply AND no MQTT connection (see beacon_discovery.py, GAIA_INTERFACE.md section 3 "LAN prima di Tailscale"). Gated by Services > Broker Auto-Discovery (off by default). No bundled UI -- bind a List COMP to devices_table per-project.'
      position: [-70, -4890]
      size: [1070, 950]
      color: [0.5, 0.35, 0.5]
    - name: annotate5
      mode: annotate
      title: Portable Export
      text: 'pre_release hook (Embody ExportPortableTox): blanks instance/project identity pars (Deviceid, Family, Stanza, opshortcut, Name) on the staged export copy only -- never touches the live component.'
      position: [-70, -5620]
      size: [270, 330]
      color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
    - name: annotate6
      mode: annotate
      title: Data Outputs (connettori del componente)
      text: 'Contratto stabile verso il progetto ospite (sw_version 1.2.0). Ordine fisso tramite connectorder, i nuovi SOLO in coda: 0 soul (CHOP, mood_r/g/b stress calm social curiosity energy lifeindex), 1 mocap (CHOP: f* viso, h* mani, p* pose = indici posizionali, non landmark semantici; faces/hands/poses conteggi), 2 status (CHOP: connected, agent_connected, mocap_active, msg_age in s, -1 = nessun messaggio), 3 words (DAT word,count), 4 word (DAT parola corrente), 5 thought (DAT ultimo pensiero). Un Out non collegato non cucina: costo zero per chi non lo usa. Non rinominare questi Out: i progetti ci si collegano.'
      position: [2330, -2270]
      size: [670, 3230]
      color: [0.35, 0.35, 0.55]
  - name: patch_panel
    type: containerCOMP
    parameters:
      w: 940
      h: 720
      bgcolorr: 0.08
      bgcolorg: 0.08
      bgcolorb: 0.1
      align: verttb
      spacing: 6
      marginl: 6
      marginr: 6
      marginb: 6
      margint: 6
    position: [-200, -1200]
    size: [160, 130]
    color: [0.325, 0.8, 0.3]
    tags:
    - tox
    children:
    - name: rigs
      type: containerCOMP
      parameters:
        hmode: fill
        vmode: fill
        bgcolorr: 0.08
        bgcolorg: 0.08
        bgcolorb: 0.1
        align: horizlr
        spacing: 6
      position: [0, -400]
      size: [160, 130]
      color: [0.325, 0.8, 0.3]
